IMPORT prelude

-- Veterinary Practice Act 2026 (Singapore) -- what counts as an animal and as veterinary practice (s 2), who is a duly qualified
-- veterinarian (s 3, and the deemed status of existing licensees under s 90), renewing a practising certificate (s 23), the offences
-- of unqualified practice and false titles (ss 29 to 36), and bringing and deciding a disciplinary case (ss 40, 42, 43, 56, 62).
--
-- Edition: the Act as enacted (No. 11 of 2026), informal consolidation, "version in force from 1/8/2026", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/VPA2026.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026, "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The deposit annotates no
-- amending Act. s 1 leaves commencement to a Gazette notification; the deposit does not say which sections are in force.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0023 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to -- here a pet owner, an
-- animal-care business, a vet or a vet student; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions such a person
-- meets. Not encoded: the Council, its members and meetings (Part 2); the registers and the tests for full, restricted and specialist
-- registration (ss 15 to 22); cancellation and restoration of registration (ss 26, 27); voluntary cancellation (ss 37, 38); the
-- Registrar's review, Complaints Assessment Committees, mediation, Interim Orders Committees and investigations (ss 44 to 55, 57 to
-- 61, 63 to 78); composition, exemption and regulations (ss 83, 86, 87); and anything "prescribed", since no regulations were read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Veterinary Practice Act 2026`

§§ `2 -- animals and the practice of veterinary medicine`

-- s 2: "animal" means "a mammal (other than a human being), a bird, a reptile, an amphibian, or a fish (including a crustacean,
-- mollusc or other aquatic invertebrate), and includes the young or egg of any animal".
-- Insects and spiders are not in the list (an inference from their absence). The text puts molluscs under "fish"; a land snail is a
-- mollusc, and this encoding reads the words literally (an inference: the parenthesis may be meant for aquatic species only).
DECLARE Creature IS ONE OF
    `a dog`
    `a cat`
    `a parrot`
    `a snake`
    `a frog`
    `a goldfish`
    `a prawn`
    `a land snail`
    `a hen's egg`
    `a butterfly`
    `a spider`
    `a human being`

GIVEN `the creature` IS A Creature
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creature is an animal` IF
    CONSIDER `the creature`
    WHEN `a butterfly` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a spider` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a human being` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 2: "practice of veterinary medicine" means any procedure, treatment, advice or attendance "usually carried out or given by
-- veterinarians, such as" (a) diagnosis, including diagnostic tests; (b) advice based on such diagnosis; (c) "medical treatment
-- (including of a dental or surgical nature)"; (d) anaesthetics; (e) prescribing; (f) certificates "that require[] or impl[y] the
-- exercise of professional veterinary judgment" -- health, vaccination, identity, age, sex, neuter status, cause of death, treatment.
-- s 29(7) "excluded act": (a) diagnosis; (b) "any treatment (of a surgical nature)"; (c) prescribing; (d) such certificates; (e) any
-- other prescribed act. Advice on a diagnosis, non-surgical treatment and anaesthetics are veterinary practice but NOT excluded acts.
-- Grooming and feeding are listed here as acts not "usually carried out" by vets: an inference, the Act does not mention them.
DECLARE VetAct IS ONE OF
    `diagnosing a disease or injury`
    `running a diagnostic test`
    `advising on a diagnosis`
    `giving non-surgical medical treatment`
    `performing surgery`
    `dental treatment`
    `administering an anaesthetic`
    `prescribing a drug`
    `issuing a vaccination certificate`
    `inoculating with veterinary biologics`
    `grooming a pet`
    `feeding a pet`

GIVEN `the act` IS A VetAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is veterinary practice` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `grooming a pet` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `feeding a pet` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Dental treatment: s 2(c) calls it medical treatment "of a dental or surgical nature"; s 29(7)(b) excludes only treatment "of a
-- surgical nature". Dental treatment is therefore treated as NOT excluded unless it is surgical (inference; not resolved by the text).
GIVEN `the act` IS A VetAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is an excluded act` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `diagnosing a disease or injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `running a diagnostic test` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `performing surgery` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `prescribing a drug` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `issuing a vaccination certificate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 and 90 -- duly qualified veterinarian`

DECLARE Individual HAS
    `is a registered veterinarian` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a valid practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registration is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `practising certificate is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held an unsuspended full or restricted licence when s 29 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months since s 29 commenced` IS A NUMBER
    `application under this Act finally refused or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a veterinary student in training` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is supervised by a duly qualified veterinarian` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an authorised officer or holds a s 55 inoculation licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a licence for scientific use of animals and complies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 3: "duly qualified veterinarian" -- "in this Act and any other written law" -- "means an individual who is a registered
-- veterinarian and has a valid practising certificate, but excludes" one whose (a) registration or (b) practising certificate "is
-- suspended under this Act".
-- s 90(1), (2): an individual who held a full or restricted licence under s 53(1) of the Animals and Birds Act 1965, not suspended
-- or revoked, immediately before s 29 commenced is "deemed ... to be a duly qualified veterinarian" until the earliest of (c) the end
-- of 12 months (or a longer prescribed period), (d) the grant of a practising certificate under this Act, (e), (f) final refusal or
-- withdrawal of the application for registration or a practising certificate. (No longer period was found prescribed: none read.)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is deemed duly qualified under s 90` IF
        `the individual`'s `held an unsuspended full or restricted licence when s 29 commenced`
    AND `the individual`'s `months since s 29 commenced` LESS THAN 12
    AND (NOT `the individual`'s `application under this Act finally refused or withdrawn`)

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a duly qualified veterinarian` IF
        (   `the individual`'s `is a registered veterinarian`
        AND `the individual`'s `has a valid practising certificate`
        AND (NOT `the individual`'s `registration is suspended`)
        AND (NOT `the individual`'s `practising certificate is suspended`)
        )
    OR  `is deemed duly qualified under s 90` `the individual`

§§ `29 -- practising veterinary medicine without qualification`

-- s 29(1): "an individual must not practise veterinary medicine in Singapore unless the individual is a duly qualified veterinarian".
-- Exceptions: (2) a veterinary student, in training, under supervision of a duly qualified veterinarian, per prescribed conditions;
-- (3) inoculation with veterinary biologics by an authorised officer or a s 55(1) Animals and Birds Act licensee; (4) keeping or using
-- an animal for a scientific purpose under an Animals and Birds Act licence; (5) any act "not being an excluded act" by an individual
-- (not suspended under Part 5) "under the supervision of a duly qualified veterinarian". (6) $50,000 or 12 months or both.
-- Prescribed acts and conditions are not modelled: no regulations were read.
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual, `the act` IS A VetAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception in s 29 applies` IF
        (`the individual`'s `is a veterinary student in training` AND `the individual`'s `is supervised by a duly qualified veterinarian`)
    OR  (`the act` EQUALS `inoculating with veterinary biologics` AND `the individual`'s `is an authorised officer or holds a s 55 inoculation licence`)
    OR  `the individual`'s `holds a licence for scientific use of animals and complies`
    OR  (   (NOT `the act is an excluded act` `the act`)
        AND `the individual`'s `is supervised by a duly qualified veterinarian`
        AND (NOT `the individual`'s `registration is suspended`)
        AND (NOT `the individual`'s `practising certificate is suspended`)
        )

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual, `the act` IS A VetAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `doing the act is an offence under s 29` IF
        `the act is veterinary practice` `the act`
    AND (NOT `is a duly qualified veterinarian` `the individual`)
    AND (NOT `an exception in s 29 applies` `the individual` `the act`)

§§ `30 to 33 -- holding out as a veterinarian`

-- s 30(1): an individual who is not a duly qualified veterinarian is guilty of an offence if he or she (a) "wilfully and falsely
-- pretends" to be one; (b) practises under the name or title of a veterinarian; (c) "takes or uses any name or title of a
-- veterinarian" or a word in any language with the same meaning; (d) uses a name, title, sign, uniform, badge ... implying
-- qualification; (e) "advertises or holds himself or herself out as a veterinarian".
-- (2): (d) does not apply to a veterinary student in supervised training. (4): for (c), (d), (e) "it is a defence ... to prove that
-- the individual acted without the intention to deceive or to gain any advantage, benefit or financial gain" for a business etc.;
-- (5) but not for (e) "in the prescribed circumstances".
DECLARE Holding IS ONE OF
    `wilfully pretending to be a vet`
    `practising under the title of vet`
    `using the title vet`
    `wearing a badge implying qualification`
    `advertising as a vet`

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the no-intent defence is available for the limb` IF
    CONSIDER `the holding`
    WHEN `using the title vet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `wearing a badge implying qualification` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `advertising as a vet` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual, `the holding` IS A Holding, `proved no intent to deceive or gain` IS A BOOLEAN, `in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holding out is an offence under s 30` IF
        (NOT `is a duly qualified veterinarian` `the individual`)
    AND (NOT (    `the holding` EQUALS `wearing a badge implying qualification`
              AND `the individual`'s `is a veterinary student in training`
              AND `the individual`'s `is supervised by a duly qualified veterinarian`))
    AND (NOT (    `the no-intent defence is available for the limb` `the holding`
              AND `proved no intent to deceive or gain`
              AND (NOT (`the holding` EQUALS `advertising as a vet` AND `in prescribed circumstances`))))

-- s 30(6): if A commits the offence "acting as an employee, an agent or a partner of another person (B), B shall also be guilty";
-- (7) $50,000 or 12 months or both; (8) B's defence: committed "without B's knowledge" AND B "has taken all reasonable precautions
-- and exercised due diligence".
GIVEN `the employee committed an offence under s 30` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employer knew` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employer took all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is guilty under s 30(6)` IF
        `the employee committed an offence under s 30`
    AND (`the employer knew` OR (NOT `the employer took all reasonable precautions`))

-- s 33(1): a registered veterinarian who "knowingly enables an individual (whether described as an assistant or otherwise) to assume
-- a title in contravention of section 30" is guilty of an offence. (2) defence: the contravention was due to mistake, reliance on
-- information, or another's act or cause beyond control, AND all reasonable precautions and due diligence.
GIVEN `knowingly enabled an assistant to assume a vet's title` IS A BOOLEAN, `the cause was mistake, reliance or beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vet is guilty under s 33` IF
        `knowingly enabled an assistant to assume a vet's title`
    AND (NOT (`the cause was mistake, reliance or beyond control` AND `took all reasonable precautions`))

§§ `25, 29 to 36 -- penalties`

-- ss 29(6), 30(3) and (7), 31(2), 32(2), 33(3), 36(2): each "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- s 25 (using unregistered qualifications or unapproved titles), s 34 (a registered vet falsely assuming the title of specialist)
-- and s 35 (representing another vet as a specialist): no offence; "may be subject to disciplinary proceedings" / "a disciplinary
-- case may be brought under Part 5".
DECLARE Provision IS ONE OF
    `s 25 unapproved qualification or title`
    `s 29 unqualified practice`
    `s 30 holding out as a vet`
    `s 30(6) employer of the offender`
    `s 31 permitting another to hold one out`
    `s 32 holding another out as a vet`
    `s 33 vet enabling an assistant`
    `s 34 false specialist title`
    `s 35 holding another out as a specialist`
    `s 36 fraudulent registration or forged certificate`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `breach is a criminal offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `s 25 unapproved qualification or title` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 34 false specialist title` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 35 holding another out as a specialist` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `breach is a criminal offence` `the provision` THEN 50000 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `breach is a criminal offence` `the provision` THEN 12 ELSE 0

§§ `23 -- practising certificate`

-- s 23(3): renewal "must be made no later than 30 days before the end of the period of validity"; (4) a later applicant "must also
-- pay ... the prescribed late application fee, if any". (9): the practising certificate "is cancelled immediately upon the
-- cancellation or suspension of" registration. (11): appeal to the Minister "within 30 days after service of the notice", "whose
-- decision is final".
GIVEN `days before expiry when applying` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the renewal application is late` IF
    `days before expiry when applying` LESS THAN 30

GIVEN `registration cancelled or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `certificate otherwise valid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practising certificate survives` IF
    `certificate otherwise valid` AND (NOT `registration cancelled or suspended`)

GIVEN `days after notice served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister is in time` IF
    `days after notice served` AT MOST 30

§§ `40, 42, 43 -- bringing a disciplinary case`

-- s 40(2): every disciplinary case must "(a) be made in writing; (b) be supported by a statutory declaration, unless the
-- disciplinary case is brought by a public officer, an officer or employee of a public authority or the Council; and (c) be
-- accompanied by any relevant document or information" in the complainant's possession.
-- (4)(b): information about "the death of any animal resulting from the conduct of a registered veterinarian in his or her
-- professional capacity" is a ground.
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `with statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN, `brought by a public officer, public authority or the Council` IS A BOOLEAN, `with relevant documents held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disciplinary case is properly made` IF
        `in writing`
    AND (`with statutory declaration` OR `brought by a public officer, public authority or the Council`)
    AND `with relevant documents held`

-- s 42(1): the Council "must not refer" a case brought "after the end of the later of" (a) 3 years after the act, conduct or
-- occurrence; (b) 3 years after "the earliest date on which the complainant had knowledge ... or could with reasonable diligence have
-- discovered it". Periods are taken in months (36) here.
-- s 43: if the period has expired, an appointed member assesses "whether it is in the public interest" to refer anyway; if so the
-- Council "must ... refer".
GIVEN `months since the conduct` IS A NUMBER, `months since the complainant knew or could have discovered it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case is within the limitation period` IF
        `months since the conduct` AT MOST 36
    OR  `months since the complainant knew or could have discovered it` AT MOST 36

GIVEN `months since the conduct` IS A NUMBER, `months since the complainant knew or could have discovered it` IS A NUMBER, `assessed to be in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case may go to the Registrar` IF
        `the case is within the limitation period` `months since the conduct` `months since the complainant knew or could have discovered it`
    OR  `assessed to be in the public interest`

§§ `56 and 62 -- Disciplinary Committee orders and appeal`

-- s 56(2): orders include "(a) cancellation"; "(b) suspension ... for a period not exceeding 3 years"; conditions; suspension or
-- cancellation of the practising certificate; "(e) imposition of a penalty not exceeding $50,000"; censure; advisory or warning;
-- undertakings; further education; mediation; any other order. (4) the case must be dismissed if no s 56(1) finding is made.
GIVEN `a s 56(1) finding was made` IS A BOOLEAN, `suspension in months` IS A NUMBER, `penalty in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is within the Committee's power` IF
        `a s 56(1) finding was made`
    AND `suspension in months` AT MOST 36
    AND `penalty in dollars` AT MOST 50000

-- s 62(1): the vet, the complainant, or the Council (if not the complainant) may "within 30 days after service of the notice"
-- appeal to the General Division of the High Court; (2) "there is no appeal from the decision of the General Division".
GIVEN `days after notice served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the High Court is in time` IF
    `days after notice served` AT MOST 30
